# Copied to <bench home>/config.env by install.sh; sourced by every script. Unset keys keep the defaults in lib.sh.

# Where model files live (default: <bench home>/models, private). A shared folder saves disk but every account that
# can write there can swap a model file, so the report's model pins then trust that folder's writers.
#MODELS_DIR=/home/shared/models/qvac-speech/bench

# Lock shared with the fabric-llm weekly bench; the run waits while the file exists or a GPU job of another user runs.
#GPU_LOCK=/tmp/gpu-bench.lock
#LOCK_WAIT_HOURS=12

# Sources. The engine follows its branch head unless ENGINE_PIN names a full commit sha. ggml is the ggml/ tree of
# qvac-fabric-llm.cpp at the commit the engine pins (GGML_REF in engines/tts/scripts/setup-ggml.sh of the engine
# checkout), so a run always builds the ggml its engine was written against; GGML_PIN (a full commit sha) or
# GGML_BRANCH (a branch head) override that for an experiment.
#ENGINE_REPO=https://github.com/tetherto/qvac-fabric-speech.cpp.git
#ENGINE_BRANCH=master
#ENGINE_PIN=
#GGML_REPO=https://github.com/tetherto/qvac-fabric-llm.cpp.git
#GGML_BRANCH=
#GGML_PIN=

# Hosts with the lab's GPU lease tool (gpu-run on PATH: RTX 5090 box, DGX Spark, Strix Halo) lock their GPUs to leased
# jobs. A run with a GPU backend there re-executes itself under one lease (gpu-run -n 1, waiting up to LOCK_WAIT_HOURS)
# and uses the GPU it is given, so GPU_INDEX applies only to hosts without the tool.
# Backends: auto picks cpu,cuda,vulkan on Linux and cpu,metal on macOS. Per machine: RTX 5090 CUDA_ARCH=120a-real;
# DGX Spark CUDA_ARCH=121a-real, CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.3, BACKENDS=cpu,cuda, MEMORY_SAMPLER=meminfo (unified
# memory, nvidia-smi reports no memory.used); Strix Halo BACKENDS=cpu,vulkan; Mac mini M4 (16 GB) cannot load MOSS-TTS:
# SKIP_FAMILIES=moss-tts-f16,moss-tts-q8_0,moss-tts-clone-f16.
#BACKENDS=auto
#CUDA_ARCH=120a-real
#CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda
#GPU_INDEX=0
#BUILD_JOBS=
#MEMORY_SAMPLER=auto
#SKIP_FAMILIES=
# macOS: a Python with the exporter requirements of engines/parakeet/scripts/requirements-coreml.txt (coremltools, torch) for the
# *-coreml families, which export the Core ML encoder sidecar of each Parakeet model once and run it on the Apple Neural Engine.
#COREML_PYTHON=/Users/you/speech-bench/coreml-venv/bin/python
# The MLX families (parakeet-mlx, mlx-whisper, mlx-audio) run only on Darwin and only on the metal backend, through the venv at
# <bench home>/mlx/venv (README, Install); no key is needed, a host without the venv reports those cells as build-failed.
# Jetson Orin (8 GB): BACKENDS=cpu,cuda,vulkan, CUDA_ARCH=87-real, MEMORY_SAMPLER=meminfo, EVICT_PAGE_CACHE=1 (CUDA allocations
# fail while the page cache is full, so the model store, build, source and dependency trees are evicted before every cell),
# SKIP_FAMILIES of the MOSS families and of every ACE-Step family but
# acestep-turbo-q8_0 (the Turbo Q8_0 render fits on the CPU and takes about 7 min per run). A family:backend entry
# skips one cell: the Turbo Q8_0 VAE decode, both Chatterbox models and the 160 s Nemotron clip exceed the device
# memory on the GPU lanes there (the Vulkan heap is smaller than the free system memory), so SKIP_FAMILIES also lists
# acestep-turbo-q8_0:cuda,acestep-turbo-q8_0:vulkan,chatterbox-mtl-clone:cuda,chatterbox-mtl-clone:vulkan,
# chatterbox-turbo:cuda,chatterbox-turbo:vulkan,nemotron-abcba:cuda,nemotron-abcba:vulkan.
#EVICT_PAGE_CACHE=0
# Extra cmake prefixes for the ggml and engine builds, separated by ";". The Vulkan backend needs the SPIRV-Headers cmake
# package (and recent Vulkan headers); a box without the Vulkan SDK or root installs them under the bench home, for example
# cmake --install of KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Headers and Vulkan-Headers with CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=~/speech-bench/deps.
#CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/home/you/speech-bench/deps

# Runs kept under <bench home>/runs.
#KEEP_RUNS=12

# E-mail is optional and off by default: the weekly artifact page is the delivery channel. To mail as well, tether.io mail is
# Google Workspace: smtp.gmail.com, port 465, a bot or personal account and an app password stored in a file with mode 0600.
#MAIL_TO=owner@tether.io,requester@tether.io
#MAIL_FROM=speech-bench@tether.io
#SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#SMTP_PORT=465
#SMTP_USER=speech-bench@tether.io
#SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE=/home/you/.config/speech-bench/smtp-password

# Optional narrative written by Claude and put above the report in the e-mail.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_FILE=/home/you/.config/speech-bench/anthropic-api-key
#NARRATIVE_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
